AB  - A vision-based horizon line detection method was developed for aviation applications. The method is based on the semantic segmentation of images from an on-board camera installed in an aircraft. Pre-trained deep convolutional neural networks were used. They were adapted using a prepared annotated training image dataset and a transfer learning technique. Several popular variants of neural networks and their fusion were considered. A new fusion method called Weighted Voting using Segmentation Quality Measures was proposed. The obtained results can be applied to the estimation of selected aircraft orientation angles. The method was evaluated using simulation data under challenging visibility conditions. The semantic segmentation of sky areas was also tested on a challenging dataset of real images, available on the Internet. The obtained results are comparable to state-of-the-art methods.
