AB  - The longitudinal impulse issue severely affects the operational safety of heavy-haul trains. The coupler yaw angle (CYA) is an important indicator for assessing longitudinal impulse. However, traditional direct CYA measurement methods suffers from low reliability problems due to the violent impact environment at the coupler connection. To address this issue, an indirect CYA identification method based on a multi-scale feature fusion technique is proposed in this paper. Firstly, through dynamics simulation and correlation analysis, the relative displacement between the car-body and the frame (RDCF) (reflect the low-frequency variation trend of the CYA) and the lateral acceleration of the car-bodies (reflect the high-frequency details of the CYA) are selected as the sensitive response data for CYA identification. By using multi-scale feature fusion technique, a weighted fusion dataset is constructed with the selected sensitive data, and the CYA is identified using an optimized deep kernel extreme learning machine (ODKELM) network. Both simulation and filed tests are conducted showing that the proposed method has more accurate identification results since it can simultaneously track trend features and detailed change features of CYA data.
