KW  - Bridge decks
KW  - Deep learning
KW  - Ground penetrating radar
KW  - Non-destructive evaluation
KW  - Rebar detection
AB  - Ground penetrating radar (GPR) is a prominent technology for non-destructive evaluation (NDE) of reinforced concrete bridge decks. However, the accurate recognition and interpretation of rebar hyperbolas remain a significant bottleneck in GPR data analysis. This study introduced a robust deep learning (DL)-based approach for automated rebar detection, aiming to enhance the efficiency of GPR data interpretation. Initially, an automatic rebar annotation module was developed to label a comprehensive dataset of 586,116 rebar annotations with minimal human effort. Consequently, the labeled dataset was used to train and evaluate several DL models, including Faster Region-Based Convolutional Neural Networks (R-CNN) with Residual Network backbones (ResNet-50 and ResNet-101), Single Shot MultiBox Detector (SSD_VGG16 and SSD_MobileNetV3), and You Only Look Once version 8 (YOLOv8). YOLOv8 outperformed other DL architectures, achieving 0.99 precision and 0.97 recall by effectively addressing challenges in detecting blurry and overlapping hyperbolas. The YOLOv8 model was integrated into a comprehensive framework for robust and automated rebar information extraction. This framework enables more frequent condition evaluations and informed maintenance decisions for concrete bridge decks.
